      --  32-byte ROM for CPU booting Holds eight 32-bit Instructions. After
      --  power-on the eight registers (BOOT_ROM0 to BOOT_ROM7, 0x20003120 to
      --  0x2000313C, the reset vector BOOT_ADDR) hold the boot stub of the
      --  silicon, which starts with csrr a0,mhartid (0xF1402573); these words
      --  are the reset values. The boot software replaces the stub with a park
      --  loop (li a0,0; csrw mip,a0; wfi; j to the start), which the register
